Conflicted in choosing what body to buy.
 Hey people,

&amp;#x200B;

So I've just sold my old camera gear and have a budget of 2.5k to find myself a new camera for video. At the moment I'm interested in the Sony a7iii, for the 120fps and run 'n gun possibilities, but I find myself conflicted. The BMPCC 4k looks amazing aswell and is quite a lot cheaper, but it does lack continuous autofocus, and I don't know how much I will need it. I'm not a cameraman, more a director that wants his own personal gear. However, to pay the bills I will most likely be filming events and such, which I imagine is a lot more work and a lot harder if you have to manual focus every little thing you want to shoot.

&amp;#x200B;

I'm wondering whether there are some more camera's that are great/mainly for video that I don't know about, aswell as advise on these two I talked about, why the one, or why the other. I know the XT-3 Fujifilm is amazing aswell, but I don't know anything about Fuji at all, I'm probably way too scared to jump into a different brand, just like that.

&amp;#x200B;

Thank you in advance!
